    "Require in all three arms the same mission ID and both physical aircraft IDs 0/1 allocated h7.5; aircraft0 books the sole P-CREW and works h7.5–8 while aircraft1 waits. At h8 aircraft0 completes/frees/releases, aircraft1 passes a same-time availability retest, receives/books the crew and starts its planned half-hour work. Require these source-bound event identities and line order, without inferring a universal tie-break.",
    "Before (DTIM0.51) and equal (DTIM0.50) must have byte-identical full model.log and report-raw.json. In each, aircraft1 completes its second subtask and releases P-CREW at h8.5 before its preparation-ended line and the joint mission-start line at h8.5. Require two-aircraft mission success/completion h9.5, both physical aircraft ready, no cancellation, and zero terminal leases/waiters. The equal-time sequence is an observed order for this frozen model.",
    "After (DTIM0.49) must cancel the same mission at h8.49 while aircraft1 remains in its started half-hour subtask. Require ordered-to-stop, task stopped, preparation ended, proportional turnround factor0.98 on aircraft1, crew freed and released, both physical aircraft returned ready at h8.49, no mission launch/success, no terminal lease or waiter. The 0.98 is the observed 0.49/0.50 partial-work ratio; no general turnround-duration law is inferred.",
    "Reconcile every cell in each of six report tables: ProblemDescription1x1, ResultSummary1x11, SystemResults72x40, StockTotalResults72x16, ResourceResults72x16, ResourceResultsTotal1x14: 5,210 per arm and 15,630 total. Independently derive the half-hour system ready/preparing/reserved/operating and crew used/waiting intervals from physical event windows, including the h8–8.5 fractional after case (System NSYMP/NSYMR about0.98, NSYRY about0.04; Resource NRUM about0.98). Stock has no issues/backorders and is equal across arms. Before/equal all six reports equal; before/after exact difference counts in listed table order are 0/4/15/0/1/1. Check summary four success fractions 1→0 and terminal ready2/crew free1.",
